      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Lab Report: Week 9 - Acoustic Resonance\"\n",
        "subtitle: \"_Chhaya Ramnani (UID: u8336188)_\"\n",
        "author: \"_Lab partners: Tsz Wing Candice Ng, Chinatsu Komada_\"\n",
        "date: \"2026-10-07\"\n",
        "format: \n",
        "  typst:\n",
        "    toc: false\n",
        "editor:\n",
        "  render-on-save: true\n",
        "jupyter: python3\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "# Imports and Functions\n",
        "\n",
        "All fits are straight lines by orthogonal distance regression, so the uncertainty on both axes is included."
      ],
      "id": "6e21303a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from dataclasses import dataclass\n",
        "from math import pi, log\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from scipy import odr\n",
        "from uncertainties import ufloat\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "@dataclass\n",
        "class odr_fit_result:\n",
        "    parameters: np.ndarray\n",
        "    parameter_errors: np.ndarray\n",
        "    r_squared: float\n",
        "    x_nom: np.ndarray\n",
        "    y_nom: np.ndarray\n",
        "    x_err: np.ndarray\n",
        "    y_err: np.ndarray\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def linear_model(p, x):\n",
        "    return p[0] * x + p[1]\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def proportional_model(p, x):\n",
        "    return p[0] * x\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def odr_fit(x, y, model_func, beta0):\n",
        "    x_nom, x_err = np.array([v.n for v in x]), np.array([v.s for v in x])\n",
        "    y_nom, y_err = np.array([v.n for v in y]), np.array([v.s for v in y])\n",
        "\n",
        "    data = odr.RealData(x_nom, y_nom, sx=x_err, sy=y_err)\n",
        "    odr_result = odr.ODR(data, odr.Model(model_func), beta0=beta0).run()\n",
        "\n",
        "    residuals = y_nom - model_func(odr_result.beta, x_nom)\n",
        "    r_squared = 1 - np.sum(residuals**2) / np.sum((y_nom - np.mean(y_nom)) ** 2)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return odr_fit_result(odr_result.beta, odr_result.sd_beta, r_squared, x_nom, y_nom, x_err, y_err)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def sigma_test(k1, sk1, k2, sk2, label=\"parameter\"):\n",
        "    sigma_diff = abs(k1 - k2) / np.sqrt(sk1**2 + sk2**2)\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nSIGMA TEST ({label})\")\n",
        "    print(f\"value 1 : {k1:.3f} +/- {sk1:.3f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"value 2 : {k2:.3f} +/- {sk2:.3f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"discrepancy: {sigma_diff:.2f} sigma -> {'AGREE' if sigma_diff <= 3 else 'DISAGREE'}\")\n",
        "    return sigma_diff\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def plot_fit(result, model_func, xlabel, ylabel, title, filename):\n",
        "    x_smooth = np.linspace(min(result.x_nom), max(result.x_nom), 200)\n",
        "    residuals = result.y_nom - model_func(result.parameters, result.x_nom)\n",
        "\n",
        "    fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(2, 1, figsize=(7, 7), sharex=True, gridspec_kw={\"height_ratios\": [3, 1]})\n",
        "    ax1.errorbar(result.x_nom, result.y_nom, xerr=result.x_err, yerr=result.y_err, fmt=\"o\", capsize=3, label=\"Data\")\n",
        "    ax1.plot(x_smooth, model_func(result.parameters, x_smooth), \"k--\", label=f\"ODR fit ($R^2$={result.r_squared:.4f})\")\n",
        "    ax1.set_ylabel(ylabel)\n",
        "    ax1.set_title(title)\n",
        "    ax1.grid(True, alpha=0.6)\n",
        "    ax1.legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "    ax2.errorbar(result.x_nom, residuals, yerr=result.y_err, fmt=\"o\", capsize=3, color=\"crimson\")\n",
        "    ax2.axhline(0, color=\"black\", linestyle=\"--\")\n",
        "    ax2.set_xlabel(xlabel)\n",
        "    ax2.set_ylabel(\"Residual\")\n",
        "    ax2.grid(True, alpha=0.6)\n",
        "\n",
        "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "    plt.savefig(f\"graphs/{filename}.png\", dpi=300)\n",
        "    plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "2045ee81",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Pre-Lab Questions\n",
        "\n",
        "## Question 2\n",
        "\n",
        "At the closed end of the pipe, air molecules cannot move freely, creating a displacement node (pressure antinode). At the open end, the air pressure is constrained to equal atmospheric pressure, creating a pressure node (displacement antinode).\n",
        "\n",
        "The effective length of an open-open pipe is\n",
        "$$L_{\\text{eff}}=L+0.6a$$\n",
        "\n",
        "standing waves inside a pipe closed at one end = odd number of $\\frac{\\lambda}{4}$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$L+0.6a=\\frac{n\\lambda}{4}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "   \n",
        "$$\\lambda_n=\\frac{4(L+0.6a)}{n}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "using $f=\\frac{c}{\\lambda}$,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$f_n=\\frac{nc}{4(L+0.6a)}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\boxed{f_n=\\frac{nc}{4(L+0.6a)}, \\quad n=1,3,5,...}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "## Question 3\n",
        "\n",
        "```{=typst}\n",
        "#figure(\n",
        "  image(\"images/q3.png\", width: 80%),\n",
        "  caption: [spectrum plotted],\n",
        ")\n",
        "```\n",
        "reading off the graph and the peak indicator, we see that the highest peak is at $1199 \\text{Hz}$.\n",
        "$$\\boxed{f_{\\text{peak}}=1199 \\text{Hz}}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "# Aim\n",
        "\n",
        "To find the speed of sound from the resonances of a pipe open at both ends and of a pipe closed at one end, and to measure the half-life and quality factor of the first three resonances of the open pipe.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Theory\n",
        "\n",
        "A pipe open at both ends has a pressure node near each end, and the closed-open pipe is derived in the pre-lab:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$f_n = \\frac{n\\,c}{2\\,(L + 1.2a)} \\quad \\text{(open-open)}, \\qquad f_n = \\frac{(2n-1)\\,c}{4\\,(L + 0.6a)} \\quad \\text{(closed-open)}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Both have the form $f = c\\,x$, so a plot of frequency against $x$ is a line through the origin with slope $c$. The theoretical speed of sound in dry air at $T$ ($^\\circ$C) is $c = 331.3 + 0.606\\,T$ m/s.\n",
        "\n",
        "Resonance intensity decays as $I_0 e^{-\\alpha t}$, a drop of 3 dB per half-life $T_{1/2}$, so the level falls linearly, $L(t) = L_0 - 3t/T_{1/2}$ and $T_{1/2} = 3/(-m)$ for slope $m$. The quality factor is $Q = \\pi f_r T_{1/2} / \\ln 2$.\n",
        "\n",
        "Two values are compared as $|k_1 - k_2| / \\sqrt{\\sigma_1^2 + \\sigma_2^2}$, and agree if this is at most $3\\sigma$.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Procedure\n",
        "\n",
        "First, we set up the PVC pipe like in the diagram, and taped the joint in the middle twice so air wouldn't leak or create unintended pressure irregularities. Then we measured the pipe's length and radius.   \n",
        "\n",
        "For the first part, we tested the open end. We clamped the pipe horizontally to a table and positioned a microphone right near the end. We recorded acoustic responses generated by claps, physical taps, and loud white noise played from a phone at the far end. We repeated the exact same procedure using the closed-end cap (which featured a small pre-drilled hole for the microphone).\n",
        "\n",
        "Finally, for the spectral analysis, we used the recording from the first open-end clap experiment, plotting spectra using 30 ms time windows. The level of each mode in a window was taken as the band level within ±25 Hz of the mode, because single-window spectra gave peaks that wandered by tens of Hz.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Results\n",
        "\n",
        "## Speed of sound\n",
        "\n",
        "Each recording (clap, tap, white noise on each pipe) is fitted for its own $c$, and the six are averaged and compared with the theoretical value."
      ],
      "id": "ec4d0434"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "L = ufloat(1.004, 0.0025)     # m, pipe length\n",
        "a = ufloat(0.043, 0.0025)     # m, pipe radius\n",
        "sigma_f = 10                  # Hz, uncertainty on one peak frequency\n",
        "T_room = ufloat(22, 1)        # deg C\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "open_data = [\n",
        "    {1: 166.6, 2: 326.5, 3: 465.6, 4: 655.1, 5: 817.8, 6: 982.3},       #clap\n",
        "    {1: 161.0, 2: 322.1, 3: 472.3},                                     #tap\n",
        "    {5: 819, 6: 982, 7: 1125},                                          #white noise\n",
        "]\n",
        "closed_data = [\n",
        "    {2: 258.3, 3: 413.9, 4: 595.5, 5: 758.9, 6: 931.2, 7: 1098.0, 8: 1263.7},   #clap\n",
        "    {2: 257.4, 3: 415.7, 4: 578.3, 6: 930.0, 8: 1240.7},                        #tap\n",
        "    {2: 259, 3: 419, 4: 590, 5: 753, 6: 930, 7: 1110, 8: 1252},                 #white noise\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "# f = c * x\n",
        "x_open = lambda modes: [n / (2 * (L + 1.2 * a)) for n in modes]\n",
        "x_closed = lambda modes: [(2 * n - 1) / (4 * (L + 0.6 * a)) for n in modes]\n",
        "\n",
        "c_methods = []\n",
        "for pipe, data, x_func in [(\"open\", open_data, x_open), (\"closed\", closed_data, x_closed)]:\n",
        "    for label, d in zip([\"clap\", \"tap\", \"white noise\"], data):\n",
        "        modes = sorted(d)\n",
        "        f = [ufloat(d[n], sigma_f) for n in modes]\n",
        "        res = odr_fit(x_func(modes), f, proportional_model, beta0=[340])\n",
        "        c = ufloat(res.parameters[0], res.parameter_errors[0])\n",
        "        print(f\"{pipe} {label}: c = {c:.2f} m/s, R^2 = {res.r_squared:.4f}\")\n",
        "        plot_fit(res, proportional_model, \"x (1/m)\", \"Resonant frequency (Hz)\",\n",
        "                 f\"{pipe.capitalize()} pipe, {label}\", f\"speed_{pipe}_{label.replace(' ', '_')}\")\n",
        "        c_methods.append(c)\n",
        "\n",
        "c_open, c_closed, c_mean = sum(c_methods[:3]) / 3, sum(c_methods[3:]) / 3, sum(c_methods) / 6\n",
        "print(f\"\\nopen pipe average: c = {c_open:.2f} m/s\")\n",
        "print(f\"closed pipe average: c = {c_closed:.2f} m/s\")\n",
        "print(f\"average of all six: c = {c_mean:.2f} m/s\")\n",
        "\n",
        "c_theory = 331.3 + 0.606 * T_room    # m/s\n",
        "print(f\"theoretical c at {T_room} C = {c_theory:.2f} m/s\")\n",
        "sigma_test(c_open.n, c_open.s, c_closed.n, c_closed.s, label=\"open vs closed\")\n",
        "sigma_test(c_mean.n, c_mean.s, c_theory.n, c_theory.s, label=\"average c vs theory\")"
      ],
      "id": "3534725b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "| Pipe | Method | $c$ (m/s) |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Open | clap | $343.51 \\pm 2.61$ |\n",
        "| Open | tap | $335.22 \\pm 2.61$ |\n",
        "| Open | white noise | $343.09 \\pm 2.21$ |\n",
        "| Closed | clap | $347.74 \\pm 0.81$ |\n",
        "| Closed | tap | $343.38 \\pm 1.90$ |\n",
        "| Closed | white noise | $347.21 \\pm 1.34$ |\n",
        "| Open average | | $340.61 \\pm 1.43$ |\n",
        "| Closed average | | $346.11 \\pm 0.82$ |\n",
        "| **Average of all six** | | $\\mathbf{343.36 \\pm 0.83}$ |\n",
        "\n",
        "The average of all six agrees with the theoretical $344.63 \\pm 0.61$ m/s at $22 \\pm 1\\,^\\circ$C ($1.25\\sigma$). The open and closed averages differ by $3.33\\sigma$, just past the cut-off.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Resonance decay"
      ],
      "id": "1db8b4da"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "decay_freqs = [166.6, 326.5, 465.6]   # Hz, open clap modes 1-3\n",
        "Dt = 0.03                     # s, window length\n",
        "sigma_t = 0.002               # s, uncertainty on each t_n\n",
        "sigma_L = 2.0                 # dB, uncertainty on one level\n",
        "\n",
        "# level (dB) of each mode in window n, t_n = n * Dt (band level within +/-25 Hz of the mode)\n",
        "decay_L = [\n",
        "    [-26.8, -28.1, -31.3, -43.7, -46.0, -53.8, -56.2],\n",
        "    [-23.5, -25.2, -35.7, -37.8, -44.4, -47.0],\n",
        "    [-27.8, -29.5, -36.2, -32.4, -41.7],\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "for i in range(3):\n",
        "    t = [ufloat(n * Dt, sigma_t) for n in range(len(decay_L[i]))]\n",
        "    L_db = [ufloat(v, sigma_L) for v in decay_L[i]]\n",
        "    res = odr_fit(t, L_db, linear_model, beta0=[-100, 0])\n",
        "    slope = ufloat(res.parameters[0], res.parameter_errors[0])\n",
        "    T_half = 3 / (-slope)\n",
        "    Q = pi * decay_freqs[i] * T_half / log(2)\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nmode {i + 1} ({decay_freqs[i]} Hz): slope = {slope:.1f} dB/s, R^2 = {res.r_squared:.4f}, \"\n",
        "          f\"T_1/2 = {T_half * 1000:.1f} ms, Q = {Q:.1f}\")\n",
        "    plot_fit(res, linear_model, \"$t_n$ (s)\", \"Level (dB)\", f\"Decay of mode {i + 1}\", f\"decay_mode{i + 1}\")"
      ],
      "id": "1a3be7b2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "| Mode | $f_r$ (Hz) | $T_{1/2}$ (ms) | $Q$ | $R^2$ |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| 1 | 166.6 | $16.3 \\pm 1.6$ | $12.3 \\pm 1.2$ | 0.956 |\n",
        "| 2 | 326.5 | $17.8 \\pm 1.8$ | $26.3 \\pm 2.6$ | 0.961 |\n",
        "| 3 | 465.6 | $29 \\pm 10$ | $62 \\pm 20$ | 0.759 |\n",
        "\n",
        "Modes 1 and 2 have about the same half-life, so $Q$ roughly doubles with frequency. Mode 3 has a longer half-life but a large uncertainty and a poor fit, and is within $1.2\\sigma$ of mode 2.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Limitations & Possible Sources of Discrepancy\n",
        "\n",
        "**1. Peak frequencies.** $\\sigma_f = 5$ Hz is an estimate, and the spectra were read at coarse resolution. Open-pipe mode 3 (about 466 to 472 Hz) sits 15 to 20 Hz below the 487 Hz expected, and the open-tap fit has only three modes. The uncertainties on $c$ are probably underestimated, which may explain the $3.33\\sigma$ open-closed difference.\n",
        "\n",
        "**2. Shared errors.** The six methods share $L$, $a$ and the pipe, so the uncertainty on their average is optimistic. A $\\pm 0.25$ cm error in $L$ alone is about 0.9 m/s, similar to the quoted $\\pm 0.83$ m/s.\n",
        "\n",
        "**3. Closed pipe mode 1.** The expected 83 Hz fundamental was left out, because the 90 to 110 Hz hump appears in every spectrum, including the open pipe's.\n",
        "\n",
        "**4. Decay.** With 30 ms windows each fit has only 5 to 7 points, and the mode 3 fit is poor.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Conclusion\n",
        "\n",
        "The average speed of sound over the six methods is $343.36 \\pm 0.83$ m/s, in agreement with the theoretical $344.63 \\pm 0.61$ m/s ($1.25\\sigma$). The open and closed pipe averages ($340.61 \\pm 1.43$ and $346.11 \\pm 0.82$ m/s) differ by $3.33\\sigma$. The first three resonances of the open pipe have half-lives of $16.3 \\pm 1.6$, $17.8 \\pm 1.8$ and $29 \\pm 10$ ms, giving $Q = 12.3 \\pm 1.2$, $26.3 \\pm 2.6$ and $62 \\pm 20$."
      ],
      "id": "c87198e4"
    }
  ],
